Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The foundation for weaving the ZI character through the product at meaningful
moments (welcome, empty states, AI actions, insights, success, alerts, milestones)
— without clutter or childishness. Infrastructure only; opt-in, nothing forced
onto existing screens.

- 9 transparent state assets under /public/characters/zi/ (welcome, thinking,
  scanning, working, pointing, success, alert, celebrate, empty).
- zi-registry.ts — the ONE source of truth for asset paths + meaning-based alt
  (no hardcoded paths anywhere).
- zi-copy.ts — ALL ZI wording in one place (empty/status/success/alert/celebrate/
  greeting), structured to later vary by role/gender/language without touching a
  component.
- <ZICharacter> — the single shared component: 9 states × 5 sizes × placements,
  decorative-by-default a11y (alt="" + aria-hidden; meaning-based alt when it
  carries text), gentle CSS-only animations that fully stop under
  prefers-reduced-motion, next/image (no layout shift).
- <ZIEmptyState> + <ZIStateCard> compositions (empty / insight / success / alert),
  real actions only (href or window CustomEvent).
- Design tokens (--zi-size-*, --zi-glow-subtle, --zi-card-*) + per-state keyframes,
  reusing ONLY existing ZONO tokens; RTL-safe.
- Proof integration: ZonoEmptyState gains an opt-in `character` prop — existing
  call sites are byte-for-byte unchanged (default renders the plain mark).

No business logic, permissions, routing or data touched.

